.TH DEEPIN-LIFERAFT 1 "July 2026" "deepin-liferaft 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepin-liferaft \- monitor memory pressure and present a force-quit dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepin-liferaft
.RI [ --hidden ]
.br
.B deepin-liferaft --self-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deepin-liferaft
monitors the current systemd user cgroup for Fedora-style systemd-oomd memory pressure and swap conditions.
When pressure remains unsafe, it freezes selected DDE application cgroups and opens a macOS-style dialog that can resume or force quit them.
.PP
Closing the dialog, stopping the service, or sending SIGTERM or SIGINT thaws every cgroup frozen by this process before exit.
The systemd user service sets
.B MemoryMin=16M
so the monitor's own cgroup keeps hard reclaim protection and can still poll PSI and raise the dialog under extreme memory pressure (requires systemd 253 or newer, and ancestor cgroups with memory.min configured, as Deepin sessions provide).
.SH WHITELIST
Whitelisted applications never appear in the dialog and are never frozen or force quit.
Entries are desktop file IDs, the same IDs parsed from cgroup unit names (for example
.B google-chrome
matches app-DDE-google\\x2dchrome@....service), one per line; blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
Three levels are merged into one set, following the vim configuration model: package defaults in
.IR /usr/share/deepin-liferaft/whitelist ,
system administrator entries in
.IR /etc/deepin-liferaft/whitelist ,
and per-user entries in
.IR ~/.config/deepin-liferaft/whitelist .
The whitelist is loaded once at startup; restart the service after editing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --hidden
Run the pressure monitor without showing the dialog at startup. This is the mode used by the systemd user service.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run built-in policy, parsing, formatting, and freezer ownership checks, then exit with status zero on success.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/deepin-liferaft.service
Systemd user service that starts the monitor with
.BR --hidden .
.TP
.I /usr/share/deepin-liferaft/whitelist
Packaged whitelist defaults. See
.BR WHITELIST .
.TP
.I /etc/deepin-liferaft/whitelist
System administrator whitelist entries.
.TP
.I ~/.config/deepin-liferaft/whitelist
Per-user whitelist entries.
.TP
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/user.slice/user-UID.slice/user@UID.service/
User cgroup from which memory pressure, reclaim, memory, and swap data are read.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
request a clean shutdown. Owned frozen cgroups are thawed before the process exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-oomd (8),
.BR systemd.resource-control (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Ston Jia <ston.jia@outlook.com>
